#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dfr-editor -- design your Touch Bar.

The preview at the top of the window is not a mock-up. It calls the same
dfrwidgets code the daemon draws the hardware with, against the same live
feeds, so what you arrange here is exactly what appears on the strip. When the
daemon is running, Live mode pushes each edit straight to it over the control
socket -- change a colour and the panel under your fingers changes with it,
before anything is saved.

Layout, theme and settings are three views over one config document, with undo
on every change and an explicit Save.
"""

